# convert-to-local.js

Converts absolute URLs (https://southendclub.com/...) to relative paths for local development. Use `--revert` to switch back for deploy.

**Run:** `node scripts/convert/convert-to-local.js` or `npm run convert:local` / `npm run convert:live`

## Layman's terms

When the site is live, links point to the real website. When you work on your computer, those same links need to point to your local files. This script flips the switch: one mode for local, one for going live. No manual find-and-replace.

## Medium understanding

Scans `Website/Pages/` and `Components/` for HTML and CSS. **Run from the repo root** — paths are root-relative, and the script now refuses to run rather than silently skipping a directory it cannot find. Replaces `https://southendclub.com/...` with relative paths (e.g. `../Pages/...`) for local dev. `--revert` converts relative paths back to absolute URLs for deploy. URL mappings are defined in the script (live path → local file path).

## Advanced

Node.js, no deps. `URL_MAPPINGS` maps live paths to local file paths. `getRelativePath()` computes relative path from each scanned file to the target. `convertToLocal()` / `convertToLive()` do in-place replacement. Processes `.html` and `.css` only. Run from project root (process.cwd()).
